│ Okay, let’s address this issue. The core problem is that resetting │
│ the primary key (uid) of an Item object through the reset() method │
│ doesn't work as expected, leading to the object being overwritten. │
│ This happens because Django’s AutoField doesn't allow setting the  │
│ primary key to None.  The AutoField is designed to auto-increment, │
│ and setting the primary key to None effectively breaks this        │
│ mechanism. The test case demonstrates this clearly.                │
│                                                                    │
│ The solution is to remove the uid = None line from the reset()     │
│ method. This will allow the AutoField to continue managing the     │
│ primary key automatically, and the save() operation will correctly │
│ update the object without overwriting it.                          │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 1                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]models/models.py[/file]                                     │
│  [original]class Item(models.Model):                               │
│  # uid = models.UUIDField(primary_key=True, default=uuid.uuid4,    │
│  editable=False)                                                   │
│  uid = models.AutoField(primary_key=True, editable=False)          │
│  def reset(self):                                                  │
│      self.uid = None                                               │
│      self.f = False[/original]                                     │
│  [patched]class Item(models.Model):                                │
│  uid = models.AutoField(primary_key=True, editable=False)          │
│  def reset(self):                                                  │
│      self.f = False[/patched]                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
